## Repository alignment protocol

For software-repository work, use `$harness-engineering` at project lifecycle
boundaries:

- initialize the smallest repository-local contract when creating a new project;
- run read-only `align` on first entry, when root guidance is missing, or after a
  material change to project shape, authorities, tooling, architecture, release
  flow, or trust boundaries;
- read the root and nearest applicable `AGENTS.md` before ordinary work in an
  aligned repository, without repeating a full audit;
- treat incomplete alignment as advisory, continue the requested task, and report
  at most one material harness improvement;
- follow external trackers, documents, spreadsheets, and providers only when the
  repository or user explicitly links or names them;
- keep model routing and delegation in user configuration, and never install
  project hooks, automations, custom agents, or external integrations implicitly.

Repository-local versioned artifacts remain authoritative for implementation.
Normal ambiguity, security, release, provider, destructive-action, and human
approval gates still apply independently of alignment status.
<!-- harness-engineering:global-contract:end -->
